WEBVTT

c1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Welcome to Temple Operations one oh one. Today we cover the daily routine of a working temple.

c2
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:14.000
The day begins at four thirty in the morning with the priest performing an abhishek of the main moorti.

c3
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:22.000
Following the bathing ritual, the deity is dressed and the first aarti of the day is performed.

c4
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:32.000
This morning aarti signals that darshan is open. Devotees may enter and offer their prayers to the deity.

c5
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:40.000
Prashad is prepared in the temple kitchen from ingredients donated the previous evening. It is consecrated before distribution.

c6
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:50.000
Volunteers who perform sewa in the kitchen must arrive by five in the morning. This is a strict rule.

c7
00:00:50.500 --> 00:01:00.000
The temple follows the panchang to schedule special abhishek days and festival aarti timings.

c8
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:12.000
Between the morning and evening ceremonies, the doors remain open for continuous darshan except during the noon rest.
